{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 92f76f36 and c8691c6a for the cutover head (05d618e2).\n\nQ-L1. Choose (b). `memberForKey` keeps its guard and reads\n`summary.definition`. It accepts a summary whose definition is a\n`platform:membership@\u003cn\u003e` name, and returns null for any other.\n`Summary.definition` already holds that name, and the summary is\nthe scope's own statement, which the caller authenticated. The\ntest roster gains `definition`.\n\nThe same rule serves every later site of this kind. Where code\nasked a summary for the kind of its own scope, it reads the\nsummary's `definition`. Apply it without a question, and list\neach site in the table of the note.\n\nQ-R1. Add no release file. The sentence goes in three places: the\nretired-room section of docs/operate-a-service.md, the\nimplementation note, and the body of the landing commit. Use this\ntext, which also covers a Worker that serves only indexed scopes\n(cc9d2940):\n\n  Rooms made before the identifier cutover are retired. An old\n  link answers `room-retired`, or 404 on a Worker that serves only\n  indexed scopes. The browser keeps its old rows and no longer\n  reads them.\n\nThe two imports stay: the \"join with config and key\" screen and\nthe supplied secret of the join path. One condition: a pasted\nconfig with `v: 1` gets the retired-home refusal of e46dd964,\nitem 5, and the screen imports nothing from it.\n\nThe NF-3 gate still waits for power. At 20:28 the machine was on\nbattery at 20 percent.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}